### Rules for NewPipeExtractor
-keep class org.mozilla.javascript.** { *; }
-keep class org.mozilla.classfile.ClassFileWriter
-dontwarn org.mozilla.javascript.tools.**
-dontwarn java.beans.*
-dontwarn javax.script.*
-dontwarn jdk.dynalink.**
-dontwarn com.google.re2j.Matcher
-dontwarn com.google.re2j.Pattern

# The extractor resolves streaming services and parsers through ServiceList and
# LinkHandlerFactory, both of which reach classes the call graph does not show as live.
# Leaving them to R8 rename/remove them breaks the fallback path only — the one that runs
# after the player endpoint has already refused an id — so the failure would look like
# "some tracks just won't download" rather than a crash. Kept wholesale on purpose.
-keep class org.schabi.newpipe.extractor.** { *; }
-dontwarn org.schabi.newpipe.extractor.**

### Rules for libbox (sing-box core, generated by gomobile)
# gomobile generates plain Java wrappers that call into Go through JNI and are looked up
# reflectively at runtime. Renaming or stripping any of these turns into a fatal
# UnsatisfiedLinkError / NoSuchMethodError on first use, so they are kept wholesale.
-keep class io.nekohasekai.libbox.** { *; }
-keep class go.** { *; }
-keepclasseswithmembernames class * {
    native <methods>;
}
-keepattributes *Annotation*, InnerClasses, EnclosingMethod, Signature
-dontwarn io.nekohasekai.libbox.**
-dontwarn go.**

### Rules for SnakeYAML (Clash subscription parsing)
# Only the SafeConstructor -> Map path is used, but the library reflects on tag classes.
-keep class org.yaml.snakeyaml.** { *; }
-dontwarn org.yaml.snakeyaml.**
